{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the donkey saw the angel of YHWH</b> – The angels of HaShem, the separate intelligences, are not perceived by the sense of sight, for they are not a body apprehensible in vision. And when they appear to prophets or to men of the holy spirit such as Daniel, they apprehend them in visions of the intellective soul when it attains the level of prophecy or the rank beneath it, but for them to be apprehended by the eyes of a beast is impossible. Therefore you may interpret <b>and the donkey saw</b> to mean that she sensed something frightening her from proceeding, and that was the angel who had gone forth to oppose him, as in the verse 'and my heart has seen much wisdom and knowledge' (Ecclesiastes 1:16), which is said concerning apprehension, not concerning visual sight. And when the miracle occurred in her and the Creator placed speech in her, she said to Balaam, 'Have I been accustomed to do thus to you?' (Numbers 22:30), but she did not know why she had now done so, for she was coerced and it was done to her thus. And consequently she did not say to him, 'Behold, the angel of HaShem is standing before me and his sword is drawn in his hand,' for her apprehension did not rise to know this at all. And Scripture says, 'and she saw the angel of YHWH and his sword was drawn in his hand' — not that she saw a sword, or even an angel, but Scripture alludes that because the angel was prepared to strike her, she was seized with great terror and it seemed to her as though people were coming to slaughter her. And if we say that the angels that appear in the likeness of men, as I mentioned in the portion of VaYera (Genesis 18:2), are apprehended even by the eyes of beasts, if so how did Balaam not see him and was he not stricken with dimness? But it is possible that He who added speech to her also added to the apprehension of her eyes, and she saw as a man. And Scripture did not mention concerning her 'and HaShem opened the eyes of the donkey,' as it mentioned concerning her master (Numbers 22:31), because the entire matter of the donkey is a great miracle like a new creation among created beings between the spheres, and it is not called mere opening of the eyes. But our Sages (Avot 5:6) do not count among the miracles anything but the opening of her mouth. And the reason for this miracle was to show Balaam 'who has made a mouth for man, or who makes him mute,' to inform him that HaShem opens the mouth of the mute, and all the more so can He silence the mouth of speakers, and He can also place words in their mouths to speak according to His will, for all is in His hand. And to warn him not to follow divination and sorcery and to curse by means of them, for he was a diviner and sorcerer."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:54.025102817Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}